<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia expects recovery in olive oil exports.</title>
<headline>Tunisia expects recovery in olive oil exports.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia expects to export up to 160,000 tonnes of olive oil in 1996/1997, trade officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Our estimates are that we will be exporting 150,000 to 160,000 tonnes,&quot; an official said.</p>
<p>This compares with only 20,000 tonnes in 1995/1996 because of a two-year drought.</p>
<p>Tunisia's output this season, which started in November, is seen at more than 250,000 tonnes, up from 60,000 in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Domestic vegetable oil consumption is estimated at between 50,000 and 60,000 tonnes. --Tunis newsroom +2161-787538</p>
